(Among the most startling revelations has been the intelligence discovered in the avian lineage, specifically) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(the corvid family \(crows, ravens, and jays\). Historically, the colloquial insult 'bird brain' reflected the assumption) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(that smaller, smooth brains lacked computational power. Yet neuroanatomists at Ruhr University Bochum uncovered that) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(corvid forebrains pack an astonishing density of neurons within a specialized area termed the nidopallium.) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(In quantitative cognitive trials, New Caledonian crows routinely fashion compound tools from disparate materials,) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(bending wire and whittling pandanus leaves into barbed hooks to extract concealed grubs.) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
() Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 11 Tf
(Paragraph C) Tj
0 -15 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Furthermore, laboratory experiments on Western scrub-jays have demonstrated 'mental time travel'--the ability) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(to remember not just what food was cached, but precisely where and when. If a scrub-jay hides perishable wax worms) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(alongside non-perishable seeds, it retrieves the perishable larvae first, switching to seeds if too much time has) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(elapsed. Remarkably, if observed by a competitor while caching, the jay will return in solitude later to re-hide its) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(stash in a new location, confirming an awareness of another individual's perspective.) Tj
