(Cognitive complexity is by no means confined to terrestrial vertebrates. In the marine biome, cephalopods--most) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(prominently octopuses and cuttlefish--exhibit an entirely divergent evolutionary trajectory toward intelligence.) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(Whereas human cognition is centralized in the cranium, two-thirds of an octopus's 500 million neurons reside) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(within its eight semi-autonomous arms. Each limb can explore, taste, and manipulate objects independently without) Tj
0 -14 Td
